## E07 interpretation (frozen)

E07 is a **protocol-bound structured association test** under a conditional
matched-pair exchangeability assumption. It does **not** eliminate the structural
fact that ME is always the first member of every pair and MI the second.
A significant E07 result does **not** by itself establish a purely physiological
execution-versus-imagery effect. Do not describe E07 as “controlling for” or
“removing” run order.

Plus-one one-sided p-value:

\[
p = \frac{1 + \#(T_{\mathrm{perm}} \ge T_{\mathrm{obs}})}{1 + N_{\mathrm{perm}}}
\]

For 1,000 completed permutations the denominator is 1001. Nested C tuning is
rerun under each permutation. Observed statistic must equal definitive E01
participant-mean balanced accuracy.

## E00–E01 test tail (frozen)

E01−E00 uses a **two-sided** participant-level paired sign-flip test.
E07 uses a **one-sided** above-null comparison. Different scientific questions;
tails are not chosen after seeing definitive results.

## E03 labeling (frozen)

Percentile ranges of participant effects are **distributional summaries**, not
confidence intervals for the mean. Mean participant effects use participant-level
bootstrap CIs. FDR is applied separately within the ROI-level family and within
the channel-level exploratory family.
